{"title":"1986 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be any positive integer not equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/0/9a01be0a3eb6f02b6553119e00f3aafbb664214e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Show that one can find distinct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> in the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/7/a579c65378e6e7f9439f90fab06c126239b3f29d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{2,5,13,d\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/e/01eb67a56d80dff75d8442b9b32a5604ba208fb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> is not a perfect square.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1986 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Given a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/1/241e6e35ad6d73fb2ef98244b0211deb2f25222a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> in the plane of the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/d/e5d7b77772e012370b1e30ce24d30325994dbdcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1A_2A_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" />. Define  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/f/78f949905a80e881b71c08169232616864e4ac75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_s=A_{s-3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"81\" height=\"15\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/2/8f2ce05c9e3b35dc417701eda80baca6f11a335b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\ge4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" />. Construct a set of points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/1/f21723ae1008684d65530b59805e664dd1c9cbb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1,P_2,P_3,\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"101\" height=\"16\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/a/6aa8a931efd29bc11a9118fbfd9b82e1ce51680f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"16\" /> is the image of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/e/76ebaba4ae3d5c911d6e31ad855d502ad88d48a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> under a rotation center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/5/775f4279110f3b9c53650b52a2754980ba974a0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"17\" /> through an angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/c/11c9f8fc24a92d0bb83c27b8a09c546cb8d60bdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120^o$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" /> clockwise for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/2/702d5171854901ff7b491b81098a45791d887c38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=0,1,2,\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" />. Prove that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/5/6650d0d51c7fa5c97f41e3d11bcab31424d49e37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{1986}=P_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" />, then the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/d/e5d7b77772e012370b1e30ce24d30325994dbdcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1A_2A_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" /> is equilateral.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1986 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>To each vertex of a regular pentagon an integer is assigned, so that the sum of all five numbers is positive. If three consecutive vertices are assigned the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> respectively, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/f/14fdb7fc1a58d1fa221727ace4b9cd7ddc35eeb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />, then the following operation is allowed: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> are replaced by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ecf792a9452e65001c1ec9db5cc5fdef082e229.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y,-y,z+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"122\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. Such an operation is performed repeatedly as long as at least one of the five numbers is negative. Determine whether this procedure necessarily comes to an end after a finite number of steps.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1986 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f642cbbd390b4882363ab6b5c2906dbf6be6cc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> be adjacent vertices of a regular <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-gon (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/586b8b4d54b09687100e453d4a9dba0f000e4cee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />) with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. A triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/2/0526e1f5ad1412706cf938657f754604e672a671.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XYZ$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, which is congruent to and initially coincides with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1e220396bf8f6704ea4a5f1745cc64ce339090b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OAB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, moves in the plane in such a way that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> each trace out the whole boundary of the polygon, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> remaining inside the polygon. Find the locus of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1986 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> defined on the non-negative reals and taking non-negative real values such that: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/b/31bcedd600afd6babb04a131ded3297e4343d51a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2)=0,f(x)\\ne0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e1280959c36db9e659089d9d5a545e0a0baf61a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le x&lt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/8/b3886b93172f93f2af16dcc44428e6d7efa63b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(xf(y))f(y)=f(x+y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"194\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b6400c6fe3f1ed70e5afd387a9686cdc3fa09531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1986 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Given a finite set of points in the plane, each with integer coordinates, is it always possible to color the points red or white so that for any straight line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> parallel to one of the coordinate axes the difference (in absolute value) between the numbers of white and red points on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is not greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1986 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_IMO\" title=\"1986 IMO\">1986 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=1&amp;cid=16&amp;year=1986\">IMO 1986 Problems on the Resources page</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\">IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_IMO\" title=\"1986 IMO\">1986 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO\" title=\"1985 IMO\">1985 IMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1986 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1986 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1986 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1986 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1986 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1986 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_IMO\" title=\"1987 IMO\">1987 IMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017153821\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.044 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 243/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 836/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 56/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6974/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.118      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.118      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14960:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017153821 and revision id 144027. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}